they are expected to follow it.</p>' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1261
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTIONS] SET [Supplemental_Info]='<p><strong>Question intent:</strong> To determine if a change management process is used to manage modifications to assets that support the critical service.</p>     <p>Change management is important in order to maintain assets in a condition that supports the resilience requirements of the critical service, and to avoid disruptions resulting from changes that were not foreseen or accounted for.  A change management process typically addresses changes such as:</p>     <p>&bull;  configuration changes (technology)</p>     <p>&bull;  software and hardware changes</p>     <p>&bull;  changes to the asset, including ownership, custodianship, and location</p>     <p>&bull;  addition or elimination of assets</p>     <p>&bull;  addition or elimination of controls</p>     <p><strong>Typical work products:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  change requests</p>     <p>&bull;  change implementation plan</p>     <p>&bull;  blackout plan</p>     <p>&bull;  change and configuration management board meeting minutes</p>     <p>&bull;  change approvals</p>     <p>&bull;  change tracking and status</p>     <p>&bull;  change documentation, including test results</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Yes" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  A change management process is used to control changes to all assets in each category.</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Incomplete" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull; A change management process is used to control changes to some assets in each category.</p>     <p><strong>Additional guidance</strong></p>     <p>Having an established process means that</p>     <p>&bull;  There are specific steps or activities that acquirer staff must complete.</p>     <p>&bull;  The process is supported by appropriate documentation. For example, there may be a documented list of internal staff that must be informed of certain changes.</p>     <p>&bull;  The acquirer''s staff is aware that the process exists and that they are expected to follow it.</p>' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1262
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTIONS] SET [Supplemental_Info]='<p><strong>Question intent:</strong> To determine whether the acquirer and suppliers jointly manage changes to assets that support the critical service.</p>     <p>Suppliers often own or have direct control of the assets that support the critical service.  In other cases, the acquirer may own the assets but a supplier may have defined obligations affecting the assets (for example, maintenance agreements or other support obligations).</p>     <p>Therefore, it is very important that the acquirer and relevant suppliers jointly coordinate changes to assets that support the critical service, as needed.</p>     <p><strong>Typical work products:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  clauses in formal agreements that govern change management</p>     <p>&bull;  integrated change documentation</p>     <p>&bull;  notes from cross-organization participation in change and configuration management board meetings</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Yes" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  For each relevant supplier, a process is implemented that ensures the acquirer and supplier coordinate changes to assets that support the critical service.</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Incomplete" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull; For some suppliers a process is implemented to coordinate changes, or the coordination of changes is inconsistent, or the practice is otherwise incomplete.</p>     <p><strong>Additional guidance</strong></p>     <p>Change procedures should ideally be part of a formal agreement that is established with a supplier.  Defining and communicating change procedures ensures that changes to assets will be handled in a controlled manner, consistent with acquirer policy, standards, and guidelines.</p>     <p>Examples of changes that may require joint coordination:</p>  <p>&bull; configuration (technology, software, information)</p>  <p>&bull; access rights</p>  <p>&bull; permissions</p>  <p>&bull; geographical location (people, technology, facilities)</p>  <p>&bull; protocols (technology)</p>  <p>&bull; software updates</p>  <p>&bull; process changes.</p>' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1263
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTIONS] SET [Supplemental_Info]='<p><strong>Question intent:</strong> To determine whether the acquirer and suppliers jointly manage changes to assets that support the critical service.</p>     <p>Suppliers often own or have direct control of the assets that support the critical service.  In other cases, the acquirer may own the assets but a supplier may have defined obligations affecting the assets (for example, maintenance agreements or other support obligations).</p>     <p>Therefore, it is very important that the acquirer and relevant suppliers jointly coordinate changes to assets that support the critical service, as needed.</p>     <p><strong>Typical work products:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  clauses in formal agreements that govern change management</p>     <p>&bull;  integrated change documentation</p>     <p>&bull;  notes from cross-organization participation in change and configuration management board meetings</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Yes" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull;  For each relevant supplier, a process is implemented that ensures the acquirer and supplier coordinate changes to assets that support the critical service.</p>     <p><strong>Criteria for "Incomplete" Response:</strong></p>     <p>&bull; For some suppliers a process is implemented to coordinate changes, or the coordination of changes is inconsistent, or the practice is otherwise incomplete.</p>     <p><strong>Additional guidance</strong></p>     <p>Change procedures should ideally be part of a formal agreement that is established with a supplier.  Defining and communicating change procedures ensures that changes to assets will be handled in a controlled manner, consistent with acquirer policy, standards, and guidelines.</p>     <p>Examples of changes that may require joint coordination:</p>  <p>&bull; configuration (technology, software, information)</p>  <p>&bull; access rights</p>  <p>&bull; permissions</p>  <p>&bull; geographical location (people, technology, facilities)</p>  <p>&bull; protocols (technology)</p>  <p>&bull; software updates</p>  <p>&bull; process changes.</p>' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1264
